  "en": "the Capitalism",
  "category": "lexical-noun",
  "tl": "le capitalisme",
  "alts": [],
  "register": "Neutral term in history and political economy; surrounding prose determines whether it is descriptive, approving, or critical.",
  "trap": "Capitalisme names the economic system, while capitaliste can be an adjective or a person; French common names of doctrines remain lowercase.",
  "example_tl": "Le capitalisme a survécu à la guerre froide en se transformant, sans pour autant réduire les inégalités que ses défenseurs promettaient d’atténuer.",
  "example_en": "Capitalism survived the Cold War by transforming itself, without thereby reducing the inequalities its defenders promised to alleviate.",
  "cloze": "{{c1::Le capitalisme}} a survécu à la guerre froide en se transformant, sans pour autant réduire les inégalités que ses défenseurs promettaient d’atténuer.",
  "note": "Retained in COLD_WAR_VOCAB under the exact-duplicate report rather than in FANCY_VOCAB. Old_back is accurate."
}
{
  "id": "it_cold_war_vocab_061",
  "en": "the Militancy",
  "category": "lexical-noun",
  "tl": "le militantisme",
  "alts": [],
  "register": "Neutral term for sustained activist or party engagement; the surrounding noun or adjective normally identifies the cause or organization.",
  "trap": "English militancy often suggests aggressiveness, whereas French militantisme can describe peaceful activism; combativité is preferable when confrontation itself is central.",
  "example_tl": "Le militantisme syndical s’est intensifié dans les mines, où les revendications salariales se mêlaient désormais à une contestation plus large du régime.",
  "example_en": "Trade-union activism intensified in the mines, where wage demands were now merging with a broader challenge to the regime.",
  "cloze": "{{c1::Le militantisme}} syndical s’est intensifié dans les mines, où les revendications salariales se mêlaient désormais à une contestation plus large du régime.",
  "note": "Old_back gives the intended French term, but the English prompt is potentially stronger; the example fixes the organized-activism sense inherited from the source sequence."
}
{
  "id": "it_cold_war_vocab_084",
  "en": "Developmentalism",
  "category": "lexical-noun",
  "tl": "le développementalisme",
  "alts": [
    "le développementisme"
  ],
  "register": "Specialist economics and political-science term for a state-led development doctrine; développementisme is a less common but established variant.",
  "trap": "Développementalisme names a doctrine or policy model, not development itself; le développement and l’aide au développement are therefore not synonyms.",
  "example_tl": "Le développementalisme brésilien associait planification étatique, protection du marché intérieur et industrialisation rapide, au nom d’une autonomie économique encore largement inachevée.",
  "example_en": "Brazilian developmentalism combined state planning, protection of the domestic market, and rapid industrialization in the name of an economic autonomy that remained largely unrealized.",
  "cloze": "{{c1::Le développementalisme}} brésilien associait planification étatique, protection du marché intérieur et industrialisation rapide, au nom d’une autonomie économique encore largement inachevée.",
  "note": "Old_back gives the accepted headword. Self-review retained développementisme only as an established variant and made the doctrine, rather than generic development, explicit."
}
{
