{
  "id": "it_cold_war_vocab_210",
  "en": "to impose",
  "category": "lexical-verb",
  "tl": "imposer quelque chose à quelqu’un",
  "alts": [],
  "register": "Neutral-formal and highly productive in political prose for sanctions, restrictions, conditions, obligations, and financial burdens.",
  "trap": "English impose sanctions on a country maps to imposer des sanctions à un pays; sur cannot mechanically replace à before the affected recipient.",
  "example_tl": "Après l’essai nucléaire, plusieurs gouvernements ont imposé de nouvelles restrictions commerciales au régime, malgré les réserves de leurs industriels les plus exposés.",
  "example_en": "After the nuclear test, several governments imposed new trade restrictions on the regime, despite reservations from the industrial firms in their countries most exposed to the measures.",
  "cloze": "Après l’essai nucléaire, plusieurs gouvernements ont {{c1::imposé}} de nouvelles restrictions commerciales {{c1::au}} régime, malgré les réserves de leurs industriels les plus exposés.",
  "note": "Old_back supplies only the verb. Self-review retained the broader political frame beyond the earlier embargo expression and clozed the inflected verb and recipient preposition separately."
}

